  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "how-this-works",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "w": 660,
      "page": "landscape",
      "text": "Every tab, in every form factor. Pages along the top switch between iPhone landscape, iPhone portrait and Web.\n\nThese are not redraws - they are the app’s own markup and stylesheet, lifted out of a real render at each size, so what you see is what it actually does. Drag things around on any board and save; tell me which ones and I’ll port them into the app.\n\nThe hatched bands are the safe areas the phone takes back: the Dynamic Island gutters down both sides in landscape, and the island strip plus home indicator in portrait. Anything sitting in one is sitting where the hardware is."
    },
    {
      "id": "data-note",
      "x": 2144,
      "y": -300,
      "w": 480,
      "page": "landscape",
      "text": "About the data on these boards:\n\n• Trainer, Overview, Kitchen and Stats draw from what is baked into the page, so they are real.\n• Music shows the disconnected state - Spotify needs a live login.\n• Calendar is seeded with sample events, since it reads iCloud through a Worker the build sandbox cannot reach.\n\nEach board is a static snapshot, so nothing scrolls or responds to clicks - content past the bottom edge is clipped exactly the way it would be before you scrolled."
    },
    {
      "id": "web-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "w": 560,
      "page": "web",
      "text": "The web boards are the desktop tier (1100px and up): the top tab bar is replaced by a left sidebar, and the columns get more room. Same app, same stylesheet - just a wider window, so no safe areas apply."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "landscape"
  }
}
